      "description": "<p>Copperline Payments builds the payout and reconciliation API that online marketplaces use to pay their sellers in 40 countries. We move about USD 2 billion a year for 150 marketplaces, and our engineering team is 30 people across four continents.</p><h3>The role</h3><p>As a Software Engineer I on the Payouts team you will build the services that schedule, batch and track payouts, and the tools our operations team uses when a bank returns one.</p><h3>Responsibilities</h3><ul><li>Build and maintain Node.js (TypeScript) services and their PostgreSQL schemas.</li><li>Write idempotent, well-tested code for money movement.</li><li>Improve our internal React tools for operations and support.</li><li>Take part in code review and blameless incident reviews.</li></ul><h3>Required</h3><ul><li>1-2 years of professional software engineering experience.</li><li>Node.js and TypeScript.</li><li>Solid SQL and an understanding of database transactions.</li></ul><h3>Preferred</h3><ul><li>Experience with payments, ledgers or financial data.</li><li>Go, Docker, or AWS.</li></ul><p>Fully remote (UTC-1 to UTC+6). USD 34,000-42,000 per year, plus a home-office budget and 24 days of leave.</p>",
